# Decisions in verdict functions that no self-test pins — LESSONS #48.
#
# harnesses/gate-mutation/mutate_gates.py forces every decision in a verdict
# function (one holding a mutation row's target) True, then False, and runs the
# harness's self-test. Each line below is a mutant that left it GREEN: either
# the gate behaves differently on some input and nothing notices, or the
# decision can never matter (an equivalent mutant); a line's `why` says which.
# The sweep fails on an unpinned decision missing from this file, and on a line
# here that no longer names one. So the file only shrinks: pin a decision with
# a fixture, then delete its line. Keys name a decision by function, source
# line and expression, never by line number; `n` numbers repeats on one line.
#
# Every line below is the baseline of 2026-09-25, when the sweep first ran, and
# says so: nobody has yet looked at which kind it is. A line added later needs a
# reason of its own: why this decision cannot, or need not, be pinned.
